+# Legacy i386 maintenance notes
+
+## Upstream base
+
+- Project: GNU Compiler Collection
+- Release: 14.3.0
+- Source: `https://gcc.gnu.org/pub/gcc/releases/gcc-14.3.0/`
+- Local upstream snapshot tag: `upstream-14.3.0`
+
+This is the compiler version used by the first validated Linux 7.1/i386
+PC-98 Buildroot toolchain. The initial source snapshot has no local GCC code
+changes. Buildroot selects the upstream i386 backend with `-march=i386` and
+`-mtune=i386`.
+
+The `upstream` branch records pristine release snapshots. Local legacy-i386
+changes belong on `main` as separate reviewable commits.
+
+## Validation baseline
+
+- Build an ELF32 static musl/BusyBox root filesystem.
+- Reject `CMPXCHG`, `XADD`, x87, SIMD, and post-i386 instructions in the
+  final BusyBox executable.
+- Require the expected `LOCK XCHG` test-and-set operations.
+- Boot qemu-pc98 with `-M pc9801 -cpu 386 -m 4736K`.
+- Mount the ext4 root, enable swap, and reach the BusyBox shell.
+
+GCC 14.4 is a follow-up upstream update and must be merged and validated
+separately from this known-working 14.3.0 baseline.
